{'symbol': 'REGN', 'date': '2022-02-11 07:50:00', 'title': 'REGENERON PRESENTS ENCOURAGING PHASE 2 RESULTS FOR HIGH-DOSE AFLIBERCEPT 8 MG IN WET AGE-RELATED MACULAR DEGENERATION AT ANGIOGENESIS MEETING', 'text': 'TARRYTOWN, N.Y., FEB. 11, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0 TRIAL MET PRIMARY SAFETY ENDPOINT AND NO NEW SAFETY SIGNALS SEEN THROUGH WEEK 44 RESULTS FAVORED AFLIBERCEPT 8 MG IN VISUAL ACUITY, DRYING AND OTHER ANATOMICAL MEASURES THROUGH WEEK 44 PHASE 3 RESULTS IN WET AGE-RELATED MACULAR DEGENERATION AND DIABETIC MACULAR EDEMA EXPECTED IN THE SECOND HALF OF 2022 REGENERON PHARMACEUTICALS, INC. (NASDAQ: REGN) TODAY ANNOUNCED RESULTS FROM ITS PHASE 2 PROOF-OF-CONCEPT TRIAL EVALUATING AN INVESTIGATIONAL 8 MG HIGH DOSE OF AFLIBERCEPT COMPARED TO THE CURRENTLY-APPROVED 2 MG DOSE OF EYLEA® (AFLIBERCEPT) INJECTION IN PATIENTS WITH WET AGE-RELATED MACULAR DEGENERATION (WET AMD).'}